  "tutorialDone": "Got it",
  "@tutorialDone": {},
  "tutorialChapter1Title": "A post travels hand to hand",
  "@tutorialChapter1Title": {},
  "tutorialChapter1Body": "Nothing here is broadcast to everyone at once. A new post is handed to a few readers in its channel. If they pass it on, it reaches the next few — for as long as people keep carrying it.",
  "@tutorialChapter1Body": {},
  "tutorialChapter2Title": "No algorithm picks for you",
  "@tutorialChapter2Title": {},
  "tutorialChapter2Body": "A conventional feed ranks everything and serves whatever holds your attention longest. Relay has no ranking model at all. What reaches you got here because people, one hop at a time, decided it was worth passing on — and it stops where they stop.",
  "@tutorialChapter2Body": {},
  "tutorialChapter2LabelConventional": "Conventional feed",
  "@tutorialChapter2LabelConventional": {},
  "tutorialChapter2LabelRelay": "Relay",
  "@tutorialChapter2LabelRelay": {},
  "tutorialChapter3Title": "You are the next hop",
  "@tutorialChapter3Title": {},
  "tutorialChapter3Body": "Every post in your feed is waiting on your call. Forward it and it travels on to readers who haven’t seen it. Drop it and its journey ends with you. Either way it leaves your queue for good — there is no scrolling past.",
  "@tutorialChapter3Body": {},
  "tutorialChapter3LabelForward": "Forward — it travels on",
  "@tutorialChapter3LabelForward": {},
  "tutorialChapter3LabelDrop": "Drop — it ends here",
  "@tutorialChapter3LabelDrop": {},
  "tutorialChapter4Title": "Attention is the currency",
  "@tutorialChapter4Title": {},
  "tutorialChapter4Body": "Reviewing other people’s posts earns you tokens. Publishing spends them. So everyone asking for attention has given some first, and there is no shortcut to buy — not with money, not by posting more.",
  "@tutorialChapter4Body": {},
  "tutorialChapter5Title": "A feed that is allowed to end",
  "@tutorialChapter5Title": {},
  "tutorialChapter5Body": "Your feed is a short queue, not an endless scroll. Sometimes it runs dry — that just means every post out there has already found its readers. It fills again by itself; there is nothing to pull or refresh.",
  "@tutorialChapter5Body": {},
